Twelve hexagons through every edge
=================================

This component recovers only the fixed source lower bound n(4,6,12)>=35.
Read twelve.tex and the complete finite record. The Moore trees leave eight
vertices and one exterior edge at the only remaining order34. Exact forest
normalization and literal graph maps cover the roots; complete ordered
incidence partitions and endpoint choices cover their possible completions.
The separately accepted initializer change preserves their literal states.

Run check.py --study STUDY --out NEW_DIRECTORY --render. Default mode repeats
both complete scientific target executions. The explicit
--reuse-recorded-targets mode rehashes and acquires their exact complete
receipts while freshly running all implementation controls, independent
oracles, sanitizers, damaged inputs, guards and native build. The historical
timeout is retained and supplies no mathematical credit. Nauty is only a
proposer; each reused graph has a checked literal adjacency bijection.
The toolchain uses nauty WORDSIZE64 and the acquired library interface.

The lower bound belongs to the cited source. This is not a new conjecture
claim, an exact count, a whole-original admission, Lean or a measurement.
